  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nIn #10212, preload for json modules is disallowed in `<link rel=preload>`. (Which will use rel=modulepreload in #10233) \nHowever, should there be an event handler (either 'error' or 'load') to indicate this `<link>` has been processed?\n\nIn current spec, the [translate a preload destination](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/links.html#translate-a-preload-destination) will return null for \"json\",\nwhich will make the [preload](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/links.html#preload) will have a null request and return in step 4.\n\n> If request is null, then return.\n\nThen back to the caller, [fetch and process the link resource](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/links.html#link-type-preload:preload),\nthe preload in step 3 doesn't call the _processResponse_ because it bailed out early, so neither the event handler 'error' nor 'load' will be called.\n\nIs this behavior correct?\n\nAs the wpt [preload-type-match.html](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/preload/preload-type-match.html#L72-L74) expects the 'load' handler for `<link rel=preload as=json>` will be called.\n\nIt looks like there's a bug either in the HTML spec or in the WPT.\n\nCCing @noamr  ",
